facetimehd-dkms (AUR, 0.7.0.2): fix build against kernel 7.2+ (strncpy removed)

Kernel 7.2 removed strncpy() entirely (six-year, 360+ patch cleanup effort,
landed June 2026). facetimehd-dkms 0.7.0.2 fails to build against it:

    fthd_v4l2.c:399: error: call to undeclared library function 'strncpy'

Fix: use the kernel's own recommended drop-in replacement, strscpy() (same
3-argument signature). Apply directly to the DKMS-registered source so it
survives module rebuilds (NOT /var/lib/dkms/.../build/, which is a scratch
copy DKMS regenerates from the registered source on every build):

    /usr/src/facetimehd-0.7.0.2/fthd_v4l2.c

Then: sudo dkms install facetimehd/0.7.0.2 -k <kernel-version>

--- a/fthd_v4l2.c
+++ b/fthd_v4l2.c
@@ -396,7 +396,7 @@
 	}

 	fmt->type = V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE;
-	strncpy(fmt->description, desc, sizeof(fmt->description));
+	strscpy(fmt->description, desc, sizeof(fmt->description));

 	return 0;
 }
